body:
For what it's worth, I think your syntax is invalid based on the [current version of the rest/spread spec](https://sebmarkbage.github.io/ecmascript-rest-spread/); trailing commas aren't allowed after rest properties, since no property could actually be added after it. (See https://github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/7297 for more info.)

``` js
class Foo {
  constructor ({
    bar,
    ...baz, // <-- trailing comma is not allowed here according to rest/spread spec
  }) {}
}
```

Does the problem go away if you remove that comma?

Yes, I can confirm this is an issue when upgrading to v3.8.0. Here is a much simpler repro example:

```
let {
  foo,
  ...otherStuff,
} = object;
```

Let me know if you need my eslint config for this.
